37],["2026-06-05",199.2],["2026-06-08",200.18],["2026-06-09",196.13],["2026-06-10",192.7],["2026-06-11",189.14],["2026-06-12",186.79],["2026-06-15",184.31],["2026-06-16",192.16],["2026-06-17",190.95],["2026-06-18",192.13],["2026-06-19",190.62],["2026-06-22",189.35],["2026-06-23",188.51],["2026-06-24",192.11],["2026-06-25",189.69],["2026-06-29",189.17],["2026-06-30",194.18],["2026-07-01",200.11],["2026-07-02",198.57],["2026-07-03",194.67],["2026-07-06",200.39],["2026-07-07",198.6],["2026-07-08",187.84],["2026-07-09",194.11],["2026-07-10",198.84]],"qtr":"Q4FY26","ratios":[{"label":"ROE %","value":"5.8%"},{"label":"ROCE %","value":"8.9%"},{"label":"D/E","value":"0.7x"},{"label":"Int cover","value":"1.6x"},{"label":"Receivable d","value":"45.3"},{"label":"Inventory d","value":"56.1"},{"label":"Payable d","value":"16.9"},{"label":"OPM %","value":"8.9%"},{"label":"Promoter %","value":"66.7%"}],"s":"KANPRPLA","sec":"Industrial Packaging & Technical Textiles (FIBC/Non-Woven)","sec2":"Capital Goods","sections":{"bull_bear":[{"body":"Debt reduction priority (Net debt INR 112 Cr); Strategic M&A (Valex Ventures UK for B2C); JV investments (Essegomma for tech); Organic capex focused on high-ROI non-woven and FIBC debottlenecking.","src":"concall","title":"Capital allocation"},{"body":"Geopolitical supply chain disruptions (Middle East/Iran) keeping PP prices elevated (new normal USD 1,200-1,350/ton); Customer inventory correction delaying volume uptake; Labor availability/skilling for stitching operations (key bottleneck); Europe dependency (56% exports) though diversified within region.","src":"concall","title":"Risks & watch-items"},{"body":"Disciplined, pragmatic, and strategically patient; emphasizing 'quality of business' over pure volume; confident in pass-through mechanisms and long-term customer stickiness; cautious on short-term order book but bullish on medium-term consumption trends.","src":"concall","title":"Management quality / tone"},{"body":"Margin driver is 'stitching minutes' not just tonnage (labor efficiency is the real constraint); DFIA reversal was a regulatory artifact, not operational failure; Non-woven uses imported fiber (no captive yarn), creating a different supply chain dynamic than FIBC; Japan strategy is about long-term diversification and first-mover branding, not immediate margin accretion.","src":"concall","title":"Non-obvious takeaways"},{"body":"- Prioritizes brownfield, fast-payback investments while maintaining balance-sheet strength and credit discipline (CRISIL ratings A2/BBB+).\n- Acquisition of UK-based Valex Ventures Ltd and formation of a 50:50 JV with Italian technology partner Essegomma S.p.A. to strengthen European presence and product development.\n- Disciplined, capability-aligned diversification into technical textiles, phased and demand-led, without compromising credit profile.","src":"deck","title":"Capital allocation policy (investor deck)"}],"business":[{"body":"FIBC: 18k tons capacity, ~83-85% utilized, core cash cow; Yarn: Moving to premium/high-performance via Essegomma JV; Non-Woven: New segment, 10k tons ultimate capacity, targeting automotive/geotextile/leatherette; Exports: Europe 56.5%, S. America 21.8%, N. America 16.9%.","src":"concall","title":"Segment / subsidiary detail"},{"body":"| Challenge | Beneficiary/Loser | Dir | Conviction | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Raw material volatility (PP prices) and inventory correction compressing short-term volumes for pure-play polymer processors. | Kanpur Plastipack Limited | beneficiary | High | Demonstrated ability to pass through 65% RM cost increase while growing PAT 68%; new non-woven segment offers 15-16% EBITDA vs current 10%, providing a structural margin re-rating catalyst as capacity commissions in Sep-Dec 2026. |","src":"concall","title":"Challenges → beneficiaries & losers"},{"body":"- ~70% of revenue from exports to 60+ countries, with Europe as the largest market, supported by an acquisition in the UK and a JV with an Italian partner to strengthen brand-led growth.\n- 80-85% repeat business from long-standing customers, with pricing driven by specifications, compliance, and customization rather than commodity volumes.\n- Positioned as a premium solutions provider, not just a supplier, leveraging global collaborations for closer customer engagement and faster product development.","src":"deck","title":"Positioning (investor deck)"},{"body":"- [Acquisition] Acquired UK-based Valex Ventures Ltd in FY26 to strengthen European export footprint and brand-led growth.\n- [Joint Venture] Formed a 50:50 JV with Essegomma S.p.A. (Italy) for technology partnership and enhanced product development.\n- [Divestiture] CPP division excluded from FY26 product mix and volume data, indicating a potential discontinuation or reclassification.","src":"deck","title":"Notable from the deck"}],"latest_quarter":[{"body":"Revenue: INR 726.7 Cr (+26.3% YoY); EBITDA: INR 74.8 Cr (10.3% margin, up from prior year); PAT: INR 38.2 Cr (+68% YoY, normalized for one-offs); Order Book: Shortened lead times (3-4 weeks vs 6-8 weeks) indicating inventory correction rather than demand collapse; Net Debt: INR 112 Cr (INR 78 Cr ST borrowings). One-offs: Q4 included INR 3.65 Cr reversal of DFIA income due to govt suspension of import duties on petrochemicals, artificially suppressing Q4 other income.","src":"concall","title":"Financial scorecard"},{"body":"Gross margins stable at 45-47% despite RM spike (PP USD 1,000 to 1,700/ton) due to per-kg price pass-through clauses; Q4 EBITDA margin 13.7% (annual 10.3%); Non-woven expected to lift blended margins long-term.","src":"concall","title":"Margins & cost dynamics"}],"outlook":[{"body":"Revenue growth: 10-15% for FY27; Margins: Sustained ~11% EBITDA (non-woven target 15-16% at steady state); Order inflow: Cautious short-term due to inventory correction, expected rebound post-price stabilization; Capex/Commissioning: Non-woven Line 1 (Sep '26), Line 2 (Dec '26); FIBC Unit 3 building complete May '26, ramping to 1,800 tons in FY27.","src":"concall","title":"Guidance"},{"body":"Lead times compressed to 3-4 weeks (from 6-8) as customers adopt 'smaller, more frequent' ordering amid high PP prices; no structural demand destruction, only inventory adjustment.","src":"concall","title":"Order book & pipeline"},{"body":"Non-woven technical textiles (INR 100-120 Cr revenue potential by FY28, 15-16% EBITDA); FIBC Unit 3 expansion (6k tons incremental over 4 years, INR 130 Cr peak revenue); B2C penetration via Valex Ventures (UK); Japan market entry (first-mover advantage).","src":"concall","title":"Growth verticals / optionality"}]},"sources":["Q4FY26 concall summary","structured quarterly financials","investor presentation (02-05-2026)","Walk-the-Talk commitments ledger"],"thesis":"Kanpur Plastipack navigated FY26 raw material volatility (PP prices up 65%) via disciplined pricing and a strategic pivot toward higher-margin non-woven technical textiles, delivering 68% PAT growth despite a one-off DFIA reversal. The imminent commissioning of non-woven capacity (Sep '26) and FIBC expansion (Unit 3) sets the stage for a structural re-rating from a pure-play FIBC exporter to a diversified technical textile solutions provider.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[{"category":"operational_metric","horizon":"H2FY26 exit","item":"FIBC capacity 18,000 tons with utilisation currently 82% (14,500 tons), expected to reach 85-86% by H2 exit.","promised":"85-86 %","quarter":"Q2FY26"},{"category":"guidance","horizon":"H2FY26","item":"H2 FY26 revenue and margins expected to remain similar to H1 (H1 EBITDA ~INR32cr).","promised":"similar to H1 INR cr / %","quarter":"Q2FY26"},{"category":"guidance","horizon":"ongoing/H2FY26","item":"H1 FY26 margins (Q2 EBITDA margin 9.8%) expected to remain sustainable and possibly move up, driven by volumes and diversification.","promised":"~9.8 sustainable %","quarter":"Q2FY26"},{"category":"guidance","horizon":"next 3 quarters (FY26)","item":"EBITDA percentages are expected to remain broadly the same over the next three quarters, with demand and order book supportive.","promised":"in line with Q1 %","quarter":"Q1FY26"},{"category":"capital_allocation","horizon":"end of FY26","item":"Company plans to cut total outstanding debt from INR190 crore to about INR125 crore by end of FY26 (term loan INR80cr->INR15cr, WC INR120cr->INR110cr).","promised":"125 INR cr","quarter":"Q1FY26"},{"category":"guidance","horizon":"FY26","item":"Valex Ventures to add a net INR4-5 crore to consolidated top line, with contributions starting from the next quarter.","promised":"4-5 INR cr","quarter":"Q1FY26"},{"category":"target","horizon":"FY26 then ongoing","item":"Valex Ventures revenue (GBP 1.1m FY25) expected at GBP 1.2-1.3m this year and to grow 5-10% every year thereafter.","promised":"1.2-1.3m this year; 5-10% growth GBP m / %","quarter":"Q1FY26"},{"category":"guidance","horizon":"ongoing/FY26","item":"Management guided that the sustainable EBITDA margin will remain between 9% and 10% going forward.","promised":"9-10 %","quarter":"Q1FY26"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"Q1FY27","item":"50-50 Essegomma JV (Taslan high-performance yarn) to reach commercial production by Q1 next FY, generating ~INR25 crore annual revenue in first couple of years.","promised":"25/yr; commercial Q1FY27 INR cr","quarter":"Q2FY26"},{"category":"strategic_priority","horizon":"next 6-12 months","item":"Grant Thornton engaged on risk/advisory to streamline processes and drive productivity; reports expected over next 6-12 months as an ongoing exercise.","promised":"6-12 months months","quarter":"Q1FY26"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"H1FY27","item":"Warehouse expansion and automation initiatives underway, expected to be completed by September (FY27).","promised":"complete by Sept date","quarter":"Q4FY26"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"H2FY27","item":"Non-woven technical textile commercial production to commence by September FY27 (first machine Sept, second machine December).","promised":"September; second Dec date","quarter":"Q4FY26"},{"category":"guidance","horizon":"FY27","item":"Q4 EBITDA margin (~11%, reported 13.69% Q4 / 10.29% FY26) expected to sustain going forward.","promised":"~11 sustain %","quarter":"Q4FY26"},{"category":"guidance","horizon":"FY27","item":"FY27 top-line growth guided at about 10% (range cited 10-15%) with margins remaining similar.","promised":"10-15 %","quarter":"Q4FY26"},{"category":"guidance","horizon":"FY27","item":"Manufacturing-segment EBITDA margin (ex-trading) of 12.17% expected to be maintained going forward.","promised":"12.17 %","quarter":"Q4FY26"},{"category":"guidance","horizon":"FY27","item":"ESSEKAN (Essegomma JV) high-performance PP yarn to generate INR20-25cr (JV sells ~INR23-25cr; KPL supplies at ~INR20cr) at ~15% EBITDA in FY27; JV capex only ~INR3cr.","promised":"20-25 rev; 15% EBITDA; 3cr capex INR cr / %","quarter":"Q4FY26"},{"category":"guidance","horizon":"FY27","item":"North America contribution (fell from 21% to 16% of exports) expected to be higher this year as market conditions normalise.","promised":"higher than 16% %","quarter":"Q4FY26"},{"category":"guidance","horizon":"H2FY26 / FY27","item":"FIBC contribution expected to rise: H2 about 15% higher than H1, and next FY about 25% (full year ~15% higher than current FY).","promised":"H2 +15%, FY27 +15-25% %","quarter":"Q2FY26"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"H1-H2 FY27","item":"Non-woven greenfield plant to be commissioned by H1 next FY (FY27) with revenue starting H2 FY27.","promised":"commission H1FY27, revenue H2FY27 date","quarter":"Q2FY26"},{"category":"capex_project","horizon":"FY27 onwards","item":"INR47 crore in FIBC Division Unit 3 (Gajner Road) adding 1,200 MT conversion capacity next year, with 6,000 MT incremental over five years (1,200 MT/year).","promised":"47cr; +1,200 MT/yr; 6,000 MT/5yr INR cr / MT","quarter":"Q2FY26"}],"open_total":45,"quarters_n